% Generate `web/src/studio/StudioAssets.jsx`: the Assets tab in the Studio properties panel,
% shown when nothing is selected. It mirrors the agent window's asset kinds and is where images
% come from now that +Image left the toolbar. Pure display + click-to-add — every mutation goes
% through the interp mutators wired in Studio (this component only calls the on* callbacks).
% Clicking an asset ADDS it to the timeline in the way that fits its kind:
%   image → image overlay · video → appended cut · music → music bed · audio → SFX at playhead
%
% Imports: `useRef, useState` from 'react'; namespace `* as api` from '../api.js';
% `IconPlay, IconMusic` from '../components/icons.jsx'. No inline styles except the one small
% margin nudge called out below. Class names are the contract with web/src/styles.css — keep them
% exact. The renders-tab behaviour is pinned by StudioAssets.test.jsx.

Module constants:
- `KINDS = ['images', 'video', 'audio', 'music', 'renders']` — the tab order. `'renders'` is NOT
  a user-uploadable kind: it surfaces the agent's HyperFrames clips (the backend's top-level
  `agent_renders` array, from {project}/hf/renders) which behave like videos on the timeline, so
  its tab has no upload dropzone.
- `HINT`: a per-kind one-line hint string — images "click to add as an overlay · or drag onto the
  timeline", video "click to append a clip · or drag onto the timeline", audio "click to drop an
  SFX at the playhead", music "click to set the music bed", renders "AI-rendered clips · click to
  append, or drag onto the timeline".

Default-export `StudioAssets({ projectId, assets, background, onAddImage, onAddClip, onAddSfx,
onSetMusic, onSetBackground, onUploadAsset })`.

State: `kind` ('images'), `dragging` (false), `inputRef` (useRef null).
- `filesFor(k)` → `k === 'renders' ? assets?.agent_renders : assets?.kinds?.[k]`, defaulting to
  `[]`. `files = filesFor(kind)`. `isVideoKind = kind === 'video' || kind === 'renders'`.
- `onPick(path)`: images → onAddImage, `isVideoKind` → onAddClip (a render IS a video clip),
  music → onSetMusic, else onAddSfx.
- `handleFiles(fl)`: when `onUploadAsset` and `fl?.length`, call `onUploadAsset(kind, fl[0])`.

Render an `aside.st-inspector.st-assets`:
- When `onSetBackground` is passed, a `<BackgroundControl projectId images={assets?.kinds?.images
  || []} background onSetBackground />` at the top.
- `<h3 className="st-insp-head">Assets</h3>`.
- `.asset-tabs`: one `button.asset-tab` per KIND (`active` when selected), onClick sets `kind`,
  label is the kind name plus ` (N)` when `filesFor(k).length` is nonzero.
- `.st-hint` showing `HINT[kind]`.
- `.asset-grid`: a `p.empty` "No {kind} yet." when `files` is empty; otherwise map `files` to a
  `div.asset-item.clickable` (key `f.path`, `title="{f.name} — click to add, or drag onto the
  timeline"`, `role="button"`, `tabIndex={0}`, `draggable`):
  - onDragStart: tag the payload kind — renders drag as `'video'` (so the timeline's drop handler
    routes them to a cut, not an image overlay), every other kind as itself. Set the DnD data on
    `'application/x-opennolan-asset'` to `JSON.stringify({ kind: dndKind, path: f.path })` and
    `effectAllowed = 'copy'`.
  - onClick → `onPick(f.path)`; onKeyDown Enter or Space → preventDefault then `onPick(f.path)`.
  - Body by kind: images → `<img>` from `api.fileUrl(projectId, f.path, f.mtime)`, alt `f.name`,
    lazy. Video kinds → `.asset-thumb.video` wrapping a muted playsInline `<video>` (same fileUrl,
    `preload="metadata"`) and a `.asset-play` span holding `<IconPlay />`. Audio/music →
    `.asset-thumb.audio` with a `.asset-audio-icon` span holding `<IconMusic size={26} />`. Then a
    `.asset-name` with `f.name`.
- Upload dropzone, only when `onUploadAsset` is passed AND `kind !== 'renders'`: a `.dropzone`
  (add `drag` while `dragging`) — click opens `inputRef`; onDragOver preventDefault + set dragging;
  onDragLeave clears it; onDrop preventDefault, clears dragging, `handleFiles(e.dataTransfer.files)`.
  Text "Drop a <strong>{kind}</strong> file here, or click to choose" plus a hidden
  `<input type="file">` (ref `inputRef`) whose onChange calls `handleFiles(e.target.files)`.

Module helper `BackgroundControl({ projectId, images, background, onSetBackground })` — the
project-wide canvas background behind ALL main clips (visible where a moved/scaled clip doesn't
cover the frame). Black by default; the user picks a solid color or any project image. Writes
`metadata.background` via `onSetBackground` (null = back to black).
- `isBlack = !background`; `isColor`/`isImage` = `background?.type` is 'color'/'image'; `colorVal`
  = `background.color` when it matches `/^#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/`, else '#000000'.
- `section.st-sec.st-bg-ctrl`: a `.st-sec-h` "Canvas background"; a `.st-bg-row` with a
  `button.st-chip` "Black" (`on` when isBlack → `onSetBackground(null)`), a `label.st-bg-swatch`
  (`on` when isColor, title "Solid color background") wrapping `<input type="color" value={colorVal}>`
  whose onChange calls `onSetBackground({ type: 'color', color: e.target.value })`, and a `.st-hint`
  "solid color" with `style={{ margin: 0 }}`.
- When `images.length`, a `.st-hint` "or use an image (covers the canvas):" and a `.st-bg-images`
  mapping each image to a `button.st-bg-img` (`on` when isImage and `background.asset_id ===
  img.path`, title `img.name`, onClick `onSetBackground({ type: 'image', asset_id: img.path })`)
  holding an `<img>` from `api.fileUrl(projectId, img.path, img.mtime)`, alt `img.name`, lazy.
